<description>
Recover the hidden 5x5 patch by rotating the scene 180 degrees and cropping the blue-mask location.

Input structure
A scene contains exactly one solid 5x5 blue mask over a larger rotationally symmetric pattern.

Rule
Locate the blue mask, rotate the whole input grid 180 degrees, and return the 5x5 patch at the mask's original bbox.

Key insight
The blue block is an occluder; the hidden pixels are supplied by the opposite 180-degree-corresponding part of the same pattern.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "visible 180-degree rotationally symmetric pattern outside the solid 5x5 blue mask",
  "dst": "region covered by the blue mask",
  "transform": "rotate the whole input grid 180 degrees and output the crop at the blue mask bbox",
  "grid_shape": "same shape as the blue mask"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 24x24 (fixed)
  output: 5x5 (fixed)
  pattern:
    description: |
      Full grid has D4 symmetry (LR, UD, transpose, anti-transpose).
      Built from top-left 12x12 quadrant Q1; other quadrants are reflections.
      Q1 = [[A, B], [B, C]] where A, B, C are 6x6 blocks, each transpose-symmetric.
      Each block is a binary pattern of {one_color, black} with density 0.44-0.83.
    block_colors: 2-3 distinct non-black non-blue colors; A and B may share a color, or B and C, or all distinct
    tiling: Q1 reflected LR -> Q2, UD -> Q3, 180 -> Q4 to fill 24x24
  blue_mask:
    shape: solid 5x5 rectangle
    placement: anywhere on grid such that mask and its 180-rotated counterpart do not overlap
    constraint: rotated counterpart region contains no blue (guaranteed by non-overlap + pattern has no blue)
  transform: rotate entire grid 180 degrees, crop 5x5 at blue mask bbox -> output
  output_content: mix of black + pattern color(s), at least 1 non-black pixel [observed], no blue

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
